{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[C]Once I lived the [E7]life of a millionaire,
[A7]Spending my money, I didn't care.
I [Dm]carried my friends out [A7]for a good time,
[Dm]Buying bootleg liquor, champagne and wine.
Then I [F]began to [D7]fall so low,
Lost all my [C]good friends, I had [A7]nowhere to go.
If I [D7]get my hands on a dollar again,
I'm gonna [G7]hang on to it till that eagle grins.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
'Cause [C]nobody knows you,
[E7]When you're down and out.
[A7]In your pocket, not one penny,
And [Dm]as for friends, you [A7]don't have any.
[Dm]When you finally get back up on your feet again,
[F]Everybody wants to [D7]be your long-lost friend.
It's [C]mighty strange, with[A7]out a doubt,
[D7]Nobody knows you
When you're [G7]down and out.
{end_of_chorus}
{x_end: C}
